                                                "example_id": "5595bbac-4c1f-4239-ab8c-ec3baf25b759",
                                                "sense_id": "82379dfa-f698-3217-abe0-862b65cda09e",
                                                "text": "The left apical 4-chamber image is used for one measurement and for a “biplane” estimate (that averages values from orthogonal planes), either the right parasternal long-axis image (the authors' preference) or the left apical 2-chamber view (shown here) is also measured. […] Either a biplane (Simpson) method of discs or a 3D volumetric rendering is used for LV volume measurements in human echocardiography laboratories."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
